<!-- ── GETTING STARTED ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="getting-started">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-rocket"></i>
        <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>What is StudySync?</h3>
        <p>
            StudySync is an AI-powered study partner matching platform built specifically for
            Computer Science students. The system analyses your learning style, academic
            interests, study habits, and availability to connect you with the most compatible
            study partners in your institution.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I create an account?</h3>
        <p>
            To create an account, click <strong>Get Started</strong> on the landing page or
            navigate to <strong>/Register</strong>. You will need to provide your full name,
            matriculation number (in the format FOC/22/000001), institutional email address,
            academic level, and a secure password. Once your account is created, you will be
            directed to the profile setup wizard.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>What is the Profile Setup Wizard?</h3>
        <p>
            The profile setup wizard is a five-step onboarding process that collects the
            information the AI matching engine needs to find your best study partners.
            The five steps are:
        </p>
        <ul class="hc-list">
            <li><strong>Step 1 — Personal Info:</strong> Your preferred study environment and primary academic motivation.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 2 — Learning Style:</strong> Your VARK learning preference (Visual, Auditory, Kinesthetic, or Read/Write) and study pace.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 3 — Study Habits:</strong> Your study consistency, collaboration mode preference, and interaction style.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 4 — Interests:</strong> The CS topics you are currently studying or interested in.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 5 — Availability:</strong> The days and time slots when you are available to study each week.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Completing all five steps results in a 100% profile completion score and ensures
            the AI engine can compute your best possible matches immediately after setup.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>Why is my profile completion less than 100%?</h3>
        <p>
            Profile completion is calculated based on how many of the five setup steps you
            have completed. If you skipped any steps during the initial setup, navigate to
            <strong>My Profile</strong> (click your avatar at the top right) and complete the
            missing sections using the tabs provided.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── AI MATCHING ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="ai-matching">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-brain"></i>
        <h2>AI Matching</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How does the AI matching work?</h3>
        <p>
            StudySync uses a cosine similarity algorithm to compute a compatibility score
            between every pair of registered students. Each student's profile is converted
            into a numerical feature vector that captures six dimensions of compatibility:
        </p>
        <ul class="hc-list">
            <li><strong>VARK Learning Style</strong> — how you prefer to absorb information (weight: 25%)</li>
            <li><strong>Academic Interests</strong> — the CS topics you have selected (weight: 30%)</li>
            <li><strong>Study Pace</strong> — how quickly you move through material (weight: 15%)</li>
            <li><strong>Collaboration Mode</strong> — whether you prefer solo, pair, or group work (weight: 10%)</li>
            <li><strong>Interaction Type</strong> — synchronous, asynchronous, or mixed sessions (weight: 10%)</li>
            <li><strong>Availability Overlap</strong> — how many of your free time slots align (weight: 10%)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The higher the cosine similarity score between two students, the higher their
            match percentage displayed on the AI Matches page.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>When are matches computed?</h3>
        <p>
            Matches are computed immediately after you complete your profile setup for the
            first time. The system also recomputes your matches whenever you update your
            profile. Additionally, the matching engine runs a full recomputation for all
            users every 24 hours to account for new registrations.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>What does the match percentage mean?</h3>
        <p>
            The match percentage is derived from the cosine similarity score between your
            profile vector and another student's profile vector. A score of 100% would
            represent a perfect overlap across all six dimensions. In practice, scores
            between 60% and 90% represent strong compatibility. Scores below 30% are
            filtered out and will not appear in your match suggestions.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>Why do I have no matches?</h3>
        <p>
            This can occur for two reasons. First, your profile may be incomplete — ensure
            your profile completion is at least 60% for the matching engine to include you
            in computations. Second, there may not yet be enough registered users with
            overlapping profiles. As more students join the platform, your match list will
            grow. You can use the filter panel on the AI Matches page to lower the minimum
            match score threshold if needed.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PARTNERSHIPS ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="partnerships">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-handshake"></i>
        <h2>Partnership Requests</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I send a partnership request?</h3>
        <p>
            Navigate to <strong>AI Matches</strong> in the sidebar. Browse through your
            recommended partners and click <strong>Send Request</strong> on any partner card.
            You can also send a request from the detail overlay that appears when you click
            on a partner card. The request will appear in the recipient's Requests page
            immediately.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I accept or decline a request?</h3>
        <p>
            Navigate to <strong>Requests</strong> in the sidebar. Under the
            <strong>Incoming Requests</strong> tab, you will see all pending requests sent
            to you. Click <strong>Accept</strong> to begin a collaboration or
            <strong>Decline</strong> to archive the request. You can also accept or decline
            directly from the notification bell dropdown at the top of any page.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>What happens after I accept a request?</h3>
        <p>
            Once a request is accepted, a partnership is created and both users gain access
            to a shared collaboration workspace. The partnership will appear in the
            <strong>Active Partnerships</strong> tab under Requests and on the
            <strong>Collaborate</strong> page.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>Can I send a request to someone who is not in my match list?</h3>
        <p>
            Currently, partnership requests can only be sent to users who appear in your
            AI-generated match list. This ensures that all partnerships are built on a
            foundation of genuine academic compatibility.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── COLLABORATE ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="collaborate">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-users"></i>
        <h2>Collaboration Workspace</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I access the collaboration workspace?</h3>
        <p>
            Click <strong>Collaborate</strong> in the sidebar to view all your active
            partnerships. Click <strong>Open Workspace</strong> on any partnership card
            to enter the dedicated collaboration space for that partner.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>What can I do in the workspace?</h3>
        <p>The collaboration workspace has three sections accessible via the tabs at the top:</p>
        <ul class="hc-list">
            <li><strong>Chat</strong> — Send and receive messages with your study partner in real time. Files can also be referenced in conversation.</li>
            <li><strong>Shared Notes</strong> — A collaborative text area where both partners can write, edit, and save study notes. Click Save to persist your notes.</li>
            <li><strong>Sessions</strong> — Schedule upcoming study sessions by providing a title, date, time, and duration. All scheduled sessions appear in the sessions list with their status.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I leave feedback for a partner?</h3>
        <p>
            Inside the collaboration workspace, click the star icon in the top-right corner
            of the chat header to open the feedback form for that partnership. You can rate
            your overall experience, as well as specific dimensions such as learning style
            alignment, communication quality, and technical proficiency. Your feedback is
            used by the AI engine to improve future match recommendations.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── FLASHCARDS ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="flashcards">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i>
        <h2>Flashcards</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I create a flashcard deck?</h3>
        <p>
            Navigate to <strong>Flashcards</strong> in the sidebar and click
            <strong>New Deck</strong>. Provide a deck title and an optional topic or
            category, then click <strong>Create Deck</strong>. Your new deck will appear
            in the deck grid immediately.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I add cards to a deck?</h3>
        <p>
            Click the <strong>Add Card</strong> button on any deck card. A modal will
            appear asking for a question (the front of the card) and an answer (the back).
            Fill in both fields and click <strong>Add Card</strong>. You can add as many
            cards to a deck as you need.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How does study mode work?</h3>
        <p>
            Click <strong>Study</strong> on any deck to enter study mode. Each card is
            displayed with the question on the front. Click the card to flip it and reveal
            the answer. After reviewing the answer, three options appear:
        </p>
        <ul class="hc-list">
            <li><strong>Still Learning</strong> — marks the card as not yet mastered and continues.</li>
            <li><strong>Skip</strong> — moves to the next card without recording a result.</li>
            <li><strong>Got It</strong> — marks the card as mastered and continues.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            At the end of the session, a summary shows how many cards you answered
            correctly. The progress bar on each deck card reflects the percentage of
            mastered cards.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>Can I delete a deck?</h3>
        <p>
            Yes. Click the trash icon on any deck card and confirm the deletion. Note that
            deleting a deck permanently removes all cards within it. This action cannot
            be undone.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── ANALYTICS ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="analytics">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-chart-bar"></i>
        <h2>Analytics</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>What does the Analytics page show?</h3>
        <p>
            The Analytics page provides a personalised overview of your activity on
            StudySync. It displays six summary metrics at the top: total partnerships,
            active partnerships, AI match suggestions, messages sent, study sessions
            scheduled, and your average feedback rating received from partners.
        </p>
        <p>
            Below the metrics, four detailed sections provide deeper insight:
        </p>
        <ul class="hc-list">
            <li><strong>Profile Completion</strong> — a visual breakdown of how complete each section of your profile is.</li>
            <li><strong>Learning Style Profile</strong> — a bar chart showing your VARK score distribution and your study preferences.</li>
            <li><strong>Academic Interests</strong> — all the CS topics you have selected displayed as tags.</li>
            <li><strong>Partnership History</strong> — a list of your recent partnerships with their status and match scores.</li>
            <li><strong>Top AI Match Scores</strong> — a ranked list of your highest-scoring AI-generated recommendations.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PROFILE ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="profile">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-user-pen"></i>
        <h2>Profile &amp; Settings</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I edit my profile?</h3>
        <p>
            Click your avatar (the circle with your initials) in the top-right corner of
            any page, or click your profile in the sidebar. This takes you to the
            <strong>My Profile</strong> page. Five tabs allow you to update different
            sections of your profile: Personal Info, Learning Style, Interests,
            Availability, and Security.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>Will updating my profile affect my matches?</h3>
        <p>
            Yes. Every time you save changes to your profile, the AI matching engine
            automatically recomputes your matches to reflect your updated preferences.
            Your new match list will be available on the AI Matches page within a few
            seconds of saving.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>Can I change my matriculation number or email?</h3>
        <p>
            Your email address can be updated from the Personal Info tab on the Profile
            page. Your matriculation number is set at registration and cannot be changed
            after account creation. If you believe your matriculation number was entered
            incorrectly, please contact your system administrator.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── SECURITY ── -->
<section class="hc-section" id="security">
    <div class="hc-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i>
        <h2>Security</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I change my password?</h3>
        <p>
            Navigate to <strong>My Profile</strong> and click the <strong>Security</strong>
            tab. Enter your current password, then your new password twice to confirm.
            Your new password must be at least 8 characters long. Click
            <strong>Update Password</strong> to save the change.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How is my data protected?</h3>
        <p>
            All passwords are hashed using the BCrypt algorithm before being stored in the
            database — your plain-text password is never saved anywhere in the system.
            Authentication is handled using JSON Web Tokens (JWT) stored in secure,
            HTTP-only cookies, which prevents them from being accessed by client-side
            scripts. All communication between the browser and the server takes place over
            HTTPS.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hc-card">
        <h3>How do I sign out?</h3>
        <p>
            Click the <strong>Logout</strong> link at the bottom of the sidebar, or click
            the settings gear icon at the top right and select <strong>Sign Out</strong>.
            This clears your session cookie and redirects you to the login page.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

@section Scripts {
    <script>
        // Smooth scroll for quick nav links
        document.querySelectorAll('.hc-quicknav-item').forEach(link => {
            link.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
                if (target) {
                    target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
                }
            });
        });
    </script>
}
